        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mia Hansen-Løve, Isabelle Huppert, Lola Créton\n- Films: Things to Come, Goodbye First Love, Something in the Air\n- Events: 66th Berlin International Film Festival\n\nFacts:\n- Goodbye First Love is a 2011 Franco-German film directed by Mia Hansen-Løve.\n- Lola Créton is known for a lead role in Goodbye First Love.\n- Lola Créton is known for a lead role in Something in the Air, a 2012 film.\n- In 2016, Mia Hansen-Løve won the Silver Bear for Best Director for Things to Come at the 66th Berlin International Film Festival.\n- Things to Come stars Isabelle Huppert as Nathalie Chazeaux, a middle-aged philosophy professor whose life is undergoing a series of separations.",
